{
  "source": ".claude/skills/telugu-jyotisha/reference.md §1 (onlinejyotish Avakahada chart, Latin syllables per pada) with the standard Devanagari Avakahada letters, which separate dental (त थ द ध न) from retroflex (ट ठ ड ढ ण) sounds that the Latin column merges.",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "notes": "consonant codes: '' (vowel-initial), k kh g gh ng c (च) ch (छ) j jh ny (ञ) T Th D Dh N (retroflex) t th d dh n (dental) p ph b bh m y r l v sh (श) Sh (ष) s h L (ళ). vowel classes: a i u e o. The spelling rules for Latin and the vowel classes for Telugu are in 'latin' and 'telugu' below; unmatched sounds use 'fallbacks'. One rule per sound for both scripts: ś (Telugu శ, Latin sh) is not in the Avakahada, so both reach ṣa / sa through fallbacks; vocalic ṛ is i in both. honorifics: a first word in this list is skipped when another word follows (శ్రీ is the script form of 'śrī'). Telugu-script cross-check against the onlinejyotish Telugu table is pending; pandit review pending.",
